WEBVTT

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:03.180
Do you have a plan to transport the goods?

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:06.320
Yeah, no problems here. You?

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:08.120
No problems here, either.

00:00:09.790 --> 00:00:11.100
You bastard!

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:12.850
Well done.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:46.410
<b>After the Shoplifter!</b>

00:01:46.610 --> 00:01:49.330
You know why we've summoned you...

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:53.710
The Drago Bureau found this along 
with a corpse that was aboard

00:01:53.710 --> 00:01:56.510
a smuggling ship headed 
toward the solar system.

00:01:58.770 --> 00:02:00.670
This mark...

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:04.010
All right, done.

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:07.220
Um... Dr. Isaac.

00:02:07.230 --> 00:02:09.580
Are the only items issued by ēlDLIVE

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:13.520
this badge, handcuffs, and the uniform
that I'm eventually going to get?

00:02:14.610 --> 00:02:16.470
Should there be anything else?

00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:18.730
Like maybe a pistol or a police baton?

00:02:18.730 --> 00:02:21.460
Distributing those things would
 just be a waste of time.

00:02:21.910 --> 00:02:24.030
Space criminals are 
fighting with capabilities

00:02:24.030 --> 00:02:27.540
that Earth's science has yet
 to even conceptualize.

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:30.240
With a much more powerful 
secret in life.

00:02:30.670 --> 00:02:34.550
The reason you were able to join ēlDLIVE 
was because you were able to show

00:02:34.550 --> 00:02:37.800
a glimpse of that power 
during the qualifying exam.

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:39.880
We did?

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:43.880
I was rather surprised myself. 
That's a pretty remarkable thing.

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:45.970
It is?

00:02:45.970 --> 00:02:48.630
I feel confidence flowing out 
of you right now, Chuta.

00:02:48.630 --> 00:02:50.890
Sh-Shut up.

00:02:50.890 --> 00:02:54.780
But what is that secret of life?

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:56.180
It's body odor.

00:02:56.610 --> 00:03:01.180
The official term for it is SPH,
 which is short for Space Pheromones.

00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:04.570
So the technique that Dolugh used 
was actually a smell?

00:03:04.570 --> 00:03:08.460
SPH is a scent that cannot be 
detected by Earthlings.

00:03:09.460 --> 00:03:10.810
Which means,

00:03:10.810 --> 00:03:14.400
when we had that escapee the other day, 
the thing that Sonokata used

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:16.910
was Misuzu Sonokata's scent?

00:03:16.910 --> 00:03:19.420
Please refrain from having 
any weird fantasies.

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:21.970
Ah, Misuzu.

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:23.800
Is mine ready?

00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:26.980
Yours is the kit with the red capsules 
on the upper right.

00:03:26.980 --> 00:03:27.850
Right.

00:03:28.660 --> 00:03:30.710
Huh? Are you sick, Sonokata?

00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:34.140
No. It's medicine that allows me 
to adapt to this environment.

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:38.100
Panties peekie-peek. Chuta's getting excited.

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:40.720
Wh-What are you talking about?! 
I didn't see any panties—

00:03:42.890 --> 00:03:44.000
You pervert!

00:03:49.450 --> 00:03:51.320
P-Pass it to me!

00:03:52.710 --> 00:03:55.750
You've become a bit more 
assertive lately, Chuta.

00:03:55.750 --> 00:03:56.370
Huh?

00:03:57.080 --> 00:04:00.580
A lot of people have been complimenting you,
 so you've gained confidence.

00:04:00.580 --> 00:04:02.900
Y-You think so?

00:04:03.320 --> 00:04:04.900
Chuta, it's heading your way!

00:04:09.350 --> 00:04:10.450
All right!

00:04:11.720 --> 00:04:12.850
<i>Crap!</i>

00:04:13.350 --> 00:04:14.500
Sympathy!

00:04:21.810 --> 00:04:23.310
<i>Dolugh?!</i>

00:04:23.310 --> 00:04:24.940
<i>Crap! Did they see you?!</i>

00:04:24.940 --> 00:04:26.230
Nice goal!

00:04:26.230 --> 00:04:29.270
That was awesome, Chuta! I'm impressed.

00:04:29.270 --> 00:04:30.950
I-It was nothing...

00:04:36.110 --> 00:04:37.910
You're in a really good mood, Chuta.

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:40.790
Well, yeah. That was a super goal.

00:04:40.790 --> 00:04:44.170
You're interacting with people
 from your class like friends now.

00:04:44.170 --> 00:04:47.800
Yeah. I guess this is how it is
 when you actually try to make friends.

00:04:48.140 --> 00:04:49.130
Shoplifter!

00:04:49.130 --> 00:04:52.140
Someone catch that gum thief!

00:04:53.970 --> 00:04:55.430
Hold it!

00:04:55.750 --> 00:04:57.980
Dolugh! Let's sew him up, 
cloak and all!

00:04:57.980 --> 00:04:58.930
Sewing him up!

00:05:01.480 --> 00:05:02.160
Huh?

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:02.850
It shattered?

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:08.480
Auntie!

00:05:08.480 --> 00:05:12.240
Aunt Mimi! Wake up, Aunt Mimi!

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:29.040
Are you sure you don't need to be 
looking after Mimi, Chuta?

00:05:29.780 --> 00:05:31.340
This is all my fault again.

00:05:32.310 --> 00:05:35.350
It's better if I don't do anything after all.

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:37.740
Chuta...

00:05:38.580 --> 00:05:40.860
Dolugh! Your body!

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:43.840
Anytime you're negative 
about yourself, Chuta,

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:47.350
you end up denying my existence, 
and my body becomes faint.

00:05:49.450 --> 00:05:53.950
Using your SPH powers in your 
everyday life on Earth

00:05:53.950 --> 00:05:56.240
is a violation of ēlDLIVE regulations.

00:05:56.520 --> 00:05:57.950
Sonokata...

00:05:57.950 --> 00:06:01.660
Powers not of Earth are that dangerous.

00:06:02.230 --> 00:06:03.790
I get it already.

00:06:03.790 --> 00:06:07.040
No. You only understand 
about thirty percent of it.

00:06:08.840 --> 00:06:15.180
I took care of this instance. 
However, you will face punishment next time.

00:06:37.100 --> 00:06:40.990
This is the depressed cooking that
you do when you're depressed, Chuta.

00:06:42.660 --> 00:06:45.640
Maybe I'll quit ēlDLIVE...

00:06:45.910 --> 00:06:51.920
Why? You've been slowly regaining confidence 
ever since you joined ēlDLIVE, Chuta.

00:06:51.920 --> 00:06:56.120
Confidence... That's exactly 
why Aunt Mimi got hurt.

00:06:57.020 --> 00:06:59.430
If I hadn't gotten involved...

00:07:06.140 --> 00:07:08.770
And after I'd decided I wouldn't anymore...

00:07:08.770 --> 00:07:10.890
I wouldn't get involved...

00:07:11.520 --> 00:07:12.900
Chuta! Chuta!

00:07:13.750 --> 00:07:16.150
Aren't you making way too much?

00:07:18.700 --> 00:07:19.650
You brought food?

00:07:18.760 --> 00:07:23.490
<i>Next week, with the theme of "school regulations," 
we'll follow a public morals committee chairman</i>

00:07:19.990 --> 00:07:23.810
It's still visiting hours, 
so you can take it up to her room.

00:07:23.490 --> 00:07:26.290
<i>who keeps a middle school in check 
in a rather unique way.</i>

00:07:23.810 --> 00:07:26.880
No... Actually, if you'd 
just take this to her.

00:07:26.290 --> 00:07:27.520
<i>Look forward to it.</i>

00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:28.010
Chuta?

00:07:29.670 --> 00:07:31.420
You came!

00:07:32.060 --> 00:07:35.770
To think that one of the shop's pillars 
would collapse from being so old.

00:07:35.770 --> 00:07:39.300
<i>Huh? Her memory's been altered...</i>

00:07:39.650 --> 00:07:43.560
But thank goodness that
it barely missed me!

00:07:43.890 --> 00:07:45.370
No, Auntie.

00:07:45.960 --> 00:07:47.840
The truth is that I—

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:50.440
What's the matter, Chuta?

00:07:52.140 --> 00:07:53.920
It would have been better

00:07:53.920 --> 00:07:56.400
if I'd been the one that got hurt, 
not you, Auntie.

00:07:57.820 --> 00:07:59.380
What are you talking about, Chuta?

00:07:59.380 --> 00:08:02.900
Huh? Well, I mean, you've got work...

00:08:02.900 --> 00:08:06.570
If you got hurt, I wouldn't be 
able to make delicious muffins!

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:12.070
It's only because you keep growing 
every day and come home to me safe

00:08:12.070 --> 00:08:14.380
that I'm even able to work hard!

00:08:14.380 --> 00:08:17.430
When you're doing well, 
I'm doing well, too.

00:08:18.780 --> 00:08:21.560
I-I'm sorry...

00:08:22.810 --> 00:08:26.940
I'm ridiculous... I was just 
brought to tears by my own words...

00:08:26.940 --> 00:08:27.970
Auntie...

00:08:28.450 --> 00:08:34.040
But you seem to be more cheerful 
lately, so that's made me happy.

00:08:38.340 --> 00:08:41.150
Mimi recognized the changes in you, Chuta.

00:08:41.150 --> 00:08:41.570
Yeah.

00:08:43.610 --> 00:08:49.090
<i>Auntie cares for me that much... 
I need to shape up more.</i>

00:08:51.490 --> 00:08:55.830
<i>So that I can protect 
Auntie and her muffins.</i>

00:08:56.430 --> 00:08:59.480
I'm becoming more visible again.

00:09:00.090 --> 00:09:01.910
I found you, chu.

00:09:03.350 --> 00:09:04.680
Sonokata...

00:09:04.680 --> 00:09:06.360
It's time for our shift.

00:09:07.750 --> 00:09:09.010
Yoyosa!

00:09:09.010 --> 00:09:10.490
Good work.

00:09:10.490 --> 00:09:12.560
Until Section Chief Madigan returns,

00:09:12.560 --> 00:09:16.130
I will continue to command 
all of you in Division 2.

00:09:16.130 --> 00:09:17.060
Yes, sir.

00:09:17.060 --> 00:09:22.480
However, there really aren't any jobs that 
you guys can do at your level right now.

00:09:23.560 --> 00:09:25.860
Go study for school, or something.

00:09:25.860 --> 00:09:26.650
Huh?

00:09:27.260 --> 00:09:29.260
Looks like we've got some time, chu.

00:09:29.260 --> 00:09:32.420
And I thought we were going to actually 
work on that one case, chu.

00:09:32.940 --> 00:09:34.000
That one case?

00:09:34.450 --> 00:09:36.040
You haven't heard?

00:09:36.040 --> 00:09:39.760
Apparently, the gum thief that showed up 
in the shopping district was an alien.

00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:40.770
Huh?

00:09:44.670 --> 00:09:48.200
Then why don't we catch the shoplifter?

00:09:48.200 --> 00:09:51.440
You seem rather forward 
suddenly. Why is that?

00:09:51.440 --> 00:09:52.780
Why?

00:09:53.580 --> 00:09:57.280
At this rate, my Auntie won't be 
able to run her shop in peace.

00:09:57.280 --> 00:09:58.510
You shouldn't do that, chu.

00:09:58.510 --> 00:10:00.500
Don't mix your personal feelings
 into an investigation, chu.

00:10:00.500 --> 00:10:02.660
Oh... I see.

00:10:03.270 --> 00:10:05.250
I think it's all right this time.

00:10:05.250 --> 00:10:06.450
Sonokata...

00:10:06.450 --> 00:10:10.710
We're not receiving assignments because
Officer Kokonose's level is too low.

00:10:10.710 --> 00:10:13.320
He can do his own investigation and level up,

00:10:13.320 --> 00:10:15.790
or die without leaving a trace.
Either would work in our favor.

00:10:15.790 --> 00:10:16.850
Wha—

00:10:18.290 --> 00:10:20.420
Never mind! I'll just do it myself!

00:10:21.440 --> 00:10:22.960
Go right ahead.

00:10:24.590 --> 00:10:28.890
I said that, but where am I
 even supposed to start?

00:10:29.260 --> 00:10:33.890
Chuta? How did ēlDLIVE find out
 the suspect was an alien?

00:10:33.890 --> 00:10:39.380
Why? It's probably because aliens and 
Earthlings are different in some way....

00:10:39.860 --> 00:10:43.190
Oh, yeah! It must be SPH!

00:10:44.320 --> 00:10:46.540
Um, pardon me.

00:10:49.370 --> 00:10:52.080
You saw it, didn't you?

00:10:52.990 --> 00:10:55.730
This unsightly form!

00:10:56.720 --> 00:10:58.960
So the moon guy has arms!

00:10:59.290 --> 00:11:04.210
You're precisely the 50,000th 
person to see my arms!

00:11:05.260 --> 00:11:07.040
That's quite a lot.

00:11:07.480 --> 00:11:08.600
What do you want?

00:11:08.600 --> 00:11:12.940
Um... I wanted to catch a shoplifting alien,

00:11:12.940 --> 00:11:15.100
so I was wondering if their 
SPH records were here...

00:11:15.100 --> 00:11:18.230
You're running your own investigation? 
You've got some nerve!

00:11:18.230 --> 00:11:22.240
U-Um, could you help me out?

00:11:22.240 --> 00:11:26.720
Hmm... I don't have much of a choice, 
since you saw my arms.

00:11:26.720 --> 00:11:29.380
Only on the condition 
that you won't tell the others.

00:11:29.380 --> 00:11:31.300
Thank you...

00:11:32.460 --> 00:11:37.410
SPH is unique to every individual, 
just like Earthlings' fingerprints.

00:11:37.410 --> 00:11:39.010
No two are alike.

00:11:39.010 --> 00:11:39.910
Huh...

00:11:39.910 --> 00:11:42.250
And so, we'll search for 
any SPH that was recorded

00:11:42.250 --> 00:11:44.720
near your house 
at the time of the shoplifting,

00:11:44.720 --> 00:11:48.870
and then compare it with this data... Hm?

00:11:49.480 --> 00:11:51.640
We got a hit! That's him!

00:11:51.640 --> 00:11:55.260
Hey. Are you sure he's just a shoplifter?

00:11:56.000 --> 00:11:57.440
What's wrong?

00:11:58.000 --> 00:11:59.440
He's...

00:12:06.780 --> 00:12:11.960
<b>Laine Brick</b>

00:12:12.390 --> 00:12:13.640
Chief Laine.

00:12:15.660 --> 00:12:19.750
The shoplifter that was in my neighborhood 
is an alien and a murderer!

00:12:20.570 --> 00:12:22.610
Who did you hear that from?

00:12:22.610 --> 00:12:24.130
Um...

00:12:24.450 --> 00:12:29.090
I spotted Officer Kokonose going into 
the SPH research office earlier.

00:12:29.090 --> 00:12:32.090
I'm surprised that Méliès helped you.

00:12:32.090 --> 00:12:36.100
Hey, now. I told you to go study, didn't I?

00:12:37.280 --> 00:12:40.480
We're in the middle of investigating 
that case right now.

00:12:40.480 --> 00:12:43.490
Um, would it be possible 
for me to participate, as well?

00:12:44.580 --> 00:12:46.360
Why do you want to go that far?

00:12:47.150 --> 00:12:50.510
Well... Because at this rate, my Auntie...

00:12:50.510 --> 00:12:54.090
Chuta! You were told not to 
involve your personal feelings!

00:12:54.090 --> 00:12:55.530
Right...

00:12:55.870 --> 00:12:59.800
Um... If we let a dangerous 
criminal run free,

00:12:59.800 --> 00:13:03.840
people wouldn't be able to continue 
to live their lives in peace.

00:13:03.840 --> 00:13:06.300
Getting innocent people involved in this

00:13:06.800 --> 00:13:10.630
is as tragic as when the rice for
 your curry turns out all mushy.

00:13:13.730 --> 00:13:15.680
Curry?

00:13:17.340 --> 00:13:18.880
Huh? Huh?

00:13:19.220 --> 00:13:20.700
Very well.

00:13:20.700 --> 00:13:21.980
Go catch him!

00:13:22.850 --> 00:13:24.150
You did it, Chuta.

00:13:24.150 --> 00:13:25.950
Are you sure about this?

00:13:25.950 --> 00:13:29.450
I thought that you were marking 
that criminal, Chief.

00:13:29.470 --> 00:13:32.400
The Chief is doing stuff on a whim again.

00:13:34.920 --> 00:13:37.660
The suspect is the Gumshoe Alien Jim.

00:13:37.660 --> 00:13:40.080
He's wanted on charges 
of larceny and murder on Earth.

00:13:40.620 --> 00:13:42.190
Judging from the crime scene,

00:13:42.170 --> 00:13:44.510
while trying to illegally 
transport resources from Earth,

00:13:44.510 --> 00:13:47.130
he apparently got in an 
argument with his partner.

00:13:47.130 --> 00:13:49.420
What was the resource he stole?

00:13:49.920 --> 00:13:51.290
Bubblegum.

00:13:51.290 --> 00:13:53.020
Bubblegum?

00:13:53.560 --> 00:13:57.650
The physical properties of a Gumshoe Alien 
are very similar to gum,

00:13:57.650 --> 00:14:01.270
and gum itself can be used as a 
powerful, high-quality tonic.

00:14:01.270 --> 00:14:03.560
He killed someone over gum?

00:14:03.560 --> 00:14:06.070
They don't have gum on the Gumshoe Planet.

00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:09.700
When things are in short supply,

00:14:09.700 --> 00:14:13.950
people who would be willing to crush 
another life to get them start to appear.

00:14:14.790 --> 00:14:16.580
Is that the only clue we have?

00:14:16.580 --> 00:14:18.380
No, there's one more.

00:14:20.210 --> 00:14:22.200
You mean the yellow truck, chu?

00:14:22.200 --> 00:14:26.430
He probably acquired it in order 
to load the gum he stole and get away.

00:14:29.040 --> 00:14:34.010
The suspect's SPH is weak. 
I can't find his location.

00:14:32.110 --> 00:14:34.590
So he usually hits the keys with his chin...

00:14:34.590 --> 00:14:37.050
We can't locate him on the 
satellite cameras, either.

00:14:37.570 --> 00:14:41.670
Wouldn't a yellow truck like this 
actually stand out quite a bit?

00:14:41.670 --> 00:14:44.510
Chuta, I see something in the windshield.

00:14:44.510 --> 00:14:45.060
Huh?

00:14:46.030 --> 00:14:48.690
Is that Mount Fuji?

00:14:50.480 --> 00:14:53.710
Analyzing the angles of Mount Fuji 
reflecting in the windshield and the sunlight.

00:14:53.710 --> 00:14:56.080
I'll narrow down the possible locations.

00:14:56.650 --> 00:14:59.450
Bingo! The Tomei Highway!

00:14:59.810 --> 00:15:01.450
Ow...

00:15:01.450 --> 00:15:03.680
He messed up again, chu.

00:15:03.680 --> 00:15:05.200
Where's the yellow truck?

00:15:06.200 --> 00:15:08.640
It doesn't look like it's 
parked around here.

00:15:09.510 --> 00:15:10.710
H-Hey!

00:15:11.860 --> 00:15:16.590
I would like you to stand by here. 
You can even sit out if you'd like.

00:15:16.590 --> 00:15:18.010
What?!

00:15:18.010 --> 00:15:19.190
If you'll excuse me.

00:15:21.860 --> 00:15:26.840
Chuta, I smell gum. It's coming 
from the thicket over there.

00:15:26.840 --> 00:15:29.310
Well, they sell gum around here, too.

00:15:29.610 --> 00:15:32.360
No, this smell is Snap Snap gum.

00:15:32.360 --> 00:15:37.280
They only sell Snap Snap gum at 
old candy shops... Oh, yeah!

00:15:38.830 --> 00:15:40.270
This is ēlDLIVE!

00:15:40.270 --> 00:15:43.430
Gumshoe Alien, surrender and come out!

00:15:44.320 --> 00:15:47.380
But how is a truck in a place like this?

00:15:48.960 --> 00:15:50.190
Ow...

00:15:51.140 --> 00:15:52.130
What the?

00:15:52.420 --> 00:15:54.040
So you finally showed up, ēlDLIVE.

00:15:54.040 --> 00:15:56.270
Chuta, it's the yellow truck!

00:15:54.430 --> 00:15:58.020
Like hell I'm going to let you 
catch me! Don't mess with me!

00:15:56.270 --> 00:16:00.140
Which means this puny alien is the suspect!

00:16:00.670 --> 00:16:02.320
You're from that one time!

00:16:02.580 --> 00:16:06.590
Because you opened a hole in my body, 
I couldn't get big anymore!

00:16:07.150 --> 00:16:09.490
I'm gonna kill you next time!

00:16:09.990 --> 00:16:11.700
Hey! Hey! Hey!

00:16:10.740 --> 00:16:13.800
Who would've thought it'd 
be an alien this size?

00:16:13.800 --> 00:16:15.950
This is the Space Police ēlDLIVE!

00:16:15.950 --> 00:16:18.150
Don't even try to struggle 
and come peacefully...

00:16:18.150 --> 00:16:19.280
Ow!

00:16:20.240 --> 00:16:21.490
Y-You... Ow!

00:16:21.320 --> 00:16:22.780
Don't mess with me!

00:16:21.490 --> 00:16:22.780
Have the right to remain si—

00:16:22.780 --> 00:16:24.200
Why, you!

00:16:27.110 --> 00:16:29.280
Is that all you've got, ēlDLIVE?

00:16:30.220 --> 00:16:32.010
What is...

00:16:32.680 --> 00:16:34.420
That's SPH.

00:16:34.800 --> 00:16:36.180
Sonokata...

00:16:36.180 --> 00:16:40.310
Normal physical attacks 
will not work against SPH.

00:16:43.960 --> 00:16:45.360
SPH...

00:16:45.790 --> 00:16:47.480
Sonokata's secretions...

00:16:47.480 --> 00:16:49.400
Your way of expressing that 
is extremely unpleasant.

00:16:49.400 --> 00:16:51.530
Er... uh...

00:16:51.530 --> 00:16:54.140
Chuta! The suspect's gone.

00:16:52.070 --> 00:16:54.150
<b>Fluffy Snap</b>

00:16:54.140 --> 00:16:55.490
No...

00:16:55.490 --> 00:16:57.580
He couldn't have gotten far, chu.

00:16:59.050 --> 00:17:01.360
You fool! You let your guard down!

00:17:01.360 --> 00:17:02.190
Sonokata!

00:17:02.190 --> 00:17:03.150
Misuzu!

00:17:04.330 --> 00:17:08.040
That's what you get! I'm just gonna 
finish her off like this.

00:17:08.040 --> 00:17:09.290
This isn't good, chu!

00:17:09.290 --> 00:17:12.910
His SPH is powerfully sticking to her,
 and I can't attack, chu!

00:17:12.910 --> 00:17:15.510
Misuzu's going to be suffocated, Chuta!

00:17:15.510 --> 00:17:17.260
You say that, but...

00:17:18.010 --> 00:17:19.130
No! Sonokata!

00:17:19.130 --> 00:17:21.590
How dare you do that, you piece of gum?!

00:17:22.780 --> 00:17:24.390
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:17:26.060 --> 00:17:28.610
Chuta! Do you remember 
what happened when there was gum

00:17:28.610 --> 00:17:30.900
on Mimi's clothes and it wouldn't come off?

00:17:33.820 --> 00:17:36.390
If we use that here, it'll work.

00:17:36.390 --> 00:17:37.680
Can you do it?

00:17:37.680 --> 00:17:40.200
If you can imagine the same thing, yes.

00:17:40.900 --> 00:17:42.540
All right, let's do it!

00:17:43.710 --> 00:17:46.700
When that happens, you should use this.

00:17:47.130 --> 00:17:48.450
Sympathy!

00:17:49.300 --> 00:17:52.960
Space Pheromone! Freezing gum off!

00:17:54.790 --> 00:17:59.830
Wha... I-It's cold... 
My body's getting harder...

00:18:02.760 --> 00:18:04.210
Sonokata!

00:18:02.760 --> 00:18:04.210
Misuzu!

00:18:05.770 --> 00:18:07.020
I'm fine.

00:18:07.400 --> 00:18:08.640
Thank goodness.

00:18:09.470 --> 00:18:12.240
I thank you for saving me.

00:18:12.240 --> 00:18:14.780
But this doesn't mean 
that I've accepted you.

00:18:15.180 --> 00:18:17.300
Wh-What the heck?

00:18:17.650 --> 00:18:20.180
This time, you're under 
arrest for sure, chu.

00:18:20.180 --> 00:18:22.540
I-I'm going to be killed...

00:18:22.540 --> 00:18:24.390
I'm not going to kill you, chu.

00:18:24.390 --> 00:18:26.870
No! No, no! I'm gonna get killed—

00:18:28.240 --> 00:18:29.620
This isn't good, chu!

00:18:29.620 --> 00:18:30.830
Take cover!

00:18:33.530 --> 00:18:35.870
There's a large SPH signal.

00:18:40.710 --> 00:18:42.290
That's a nice smell.

00:18:45.440 --> 00:18:48.220
S-So close!

00:18:50.290 --> 00:18:52.130
I've repaid my debt to you.

00:18:52.480 --> 00:18:55.520
Please do not hold the fact that 
you saved me against me anymore.

00:18:55.520 --> 00:18:57.620
L-Like I would do that!

00:18:57.620 --> 00:19:00.040
Both of you! Look over there, chu!

00:19:02.990 --> 00:19:04.180
That's...

00:19:05.180 --> 00:19:07.080
So that mark was...

00:19:07.410 --> 00:19:08.690
Yeah.

00:19:08.690 --> 00:19:12.560
He was killed as a warning to others.

00:19:13.960 --> 00:19:16.510
<i>The giant criminal organization 
that commits</i>

00:19:16.510 --> 00:19:18.290
<i>all kinds of heinous crimes across this galaxy...</i>

00:19:18.580 --> 00:19:19.790
<i>DeMille.</i>

00:19:20.120 --> 00:19:21.260
DeMille?

00:19:21.710 --> 00:19:26.640
<i>Long ago, another blue, Earth-like planet 
20,000 light years away</i>

00:19:26.640 --> 00:19:28.420
<i>ended up like this because of them.</i>

00:19:29.350 --> 00:19:31.560
Something that dangerous 
is heading to Earth?

00:19:36.780 --> 00:19:39.770
Auntie, I brought you a change of clothes, 
since you're being discharged.

00:19:40.150 --> 00:19:40.940
Yo.

00:19:40.940 --> 00:19:42.860
Tateyan! Why are you...

00:19:43.260 --> 00:19:45.500
The lady from the candy shop told me.

00:19:45.500 --> 00:19:48.110
He brought me some rice crackers 
as a get well gift.

00:19:48.440 --> 00:19:50.730
Th-Thanks.

00:19:52.620 --> 00:19:56.830
Do people tell your aunt that she 
looks like the idol Yui Sakuraebi?

00:19:56.830 --> 00:19:59.460
I don't think so...

00:19:59.460 --> 00:20:00.580
I see.

00:20:00.960 --> 00:20:06.840
By the way, Chuta, I had a dream 
the other day where I think you saved me.

00:20:06.840 --> 00:20:07.710
A dream?

00:20:08.270 --> 00:20:11.080
ēlDLIVE must've changed his memories.

00:20:11.680 --> 00:20:15.890
If you thought it was a dream, 
it probably was.

00:20:16.180 --> 00:20:20.630
I see. It must've been a dream. 
You're so deep, Chuta.

00:20:20.630 --> 00:20:22.060
And you're dense, Tateyan.

00:20:22.060 --> 00:20:22.780
Shh!

00:20:23.070 --> 00:20:26.770
But thanks anyway. I wanted to tell 
you that, even if it was a dream.

00:20:28.110 --> 00:20:32.780
This feeling... You're starting 
to accept yourself more, Chuta.

00:20:32.780 --> 00:20:35.350
You don't need to comment on it every time!

00:20:36.870 --> 00:20:38.580
A-Auntie!

00:20:40.180 --> 00:20:43.360
Chuta finally made a friend!

00:20:43.360 --> 00:20:44.960
You're overreacting, Auntie!

00:20:44.960 --> 00:20:46.800
She's not, though.

00:20:48.150 --> 00:20:52.360
Ever since that incident, 
up until you joined ēlDLIVE recently,

00:20:52.360 --> 00:20:54.660
you haven't had any friends, Chuta.

00:20:54.970 --> 00:20:58.020
<i>That's right... I'd forgotten.</i>

00:20:59.270 --> 00:21:02.320
<i>This is what having friends is like.</i>

00:21:03.790 --> 00:21:07.980
<i>I think I've started realizing 
a lot of things lately.</i>

00:21:08.540 --> 00:21:12.740
<i>About my family, the people
around me, as well as myself....</i>

00:21:13.410 --> 00:21:18.600
<i>Considering all that, maybe there was 
a purpose to me joining ēlDLIVE.</i>

00:21:20.900 --> 00:21:22.970
You look all official now.

00:21:22.970 --> 00:21:24.760
It looks pretty good on you.

00:21:24.760 --> 00:21:28.310
I like it! It's a very unique outfit, Chuta.

00:21:28.310 --> 00:21:31.000
Please don't come to school wearing that.

00:21:31.000 --> 00:21:32.630
I know that!

00:21:32.630 --> 00:21:35.820
All right, let's have an 
entrance ceremony for Chuta.

00:21:35.820 --> 00:21:37.350
Yoyosa!

00:21:38.160 --> 00:21:40.560
Commencing super high-speed navigation.

00:21:40.560 --> 00:21:41.860
Is that okay, Captain?

00:21:41.860 --> 00:21:43.080
Yeah.

00:21:43.080 --> 00:21:46.780
Our target is on the blue planet in the 
solar system in the Milky Way galaxy.

00:21:46.780 --> 00:21:49.940
It's Shirobori Middle School. Right, Captain?

00:21:51.030 --> 00:21:54.710
Yeah. I can't wait to see him.

00:23:26.040 --> 00:23:27.140
There's no doubt about it.

00:23:27.140 --> 00:23:27.730
Yeah.

00:23:27.730 --> 00:23:28.560
You're right.

00:23:28.560 --> 00:23:30.800
Officer's Kokonose's naming sense is...

00:23:30.800 --> 00:23:31.750
...zero!

00:23:31.750 --> 00:23:33.300
Next time on <i>ēlDLIVE,</i>

00:23:33.300 --> 00:23:35.880
"A Pursuer From the Past: Part 1."

00:23:33.600 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>Next Time
A Pursuer From the Past: Part 1</b>

00:23:35.880 --> 00:23:38.340
Take this! Freezing gum off!
